1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,774
The Contact Center settings hold the rules that apply to every queue and every agent.

2
00:00:06,774 --> 00:00:10,962
This video shows why they exist, and walks through each tab:

3
00:00:10,962 --> 00:00:17,370
default numbers, call recording and consent, outside transfer numbers, and secure data capture.

4
00:00:21,970 --> 00:00:25,711
Some rules cannot be left to each queue or each agent.

5
00:00:25,711 --> 00:00:30,013
Whether a call is recorded, and what the caller is told, has to

6
00:00:30,013 --> 00:00:32,070
be the same for every call.

7
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:36,837
Agents need a number to call and text from, and a safe list

8
00:00:36,837 --> 00:00:39,680
of outside numbers they may transfer to.

9
00:00:40,430 --> 00:00:44,256
And when a customer reads out a card number, nobody on your team

10
00:00:44,256 --> 00:00:45,950
should hear it or see it.

11
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:51,774
The Contact Center settings page holds all of this in one place, in four tabs.

12
00:00:51,774 --> 00:00:55,700
A tab appears only when the feature behind it is turned on.

13
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:01,898
Open Settings, Contact Center.

14
00:01:01,898 --> 00:01:05,963
The Default numbers tab picks the numbers used for an agent who has

15
00:01:05,963 --> 00:01:07,300
none of their own.

16
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,973
The lists show your Omnichannel Addresses.

17
00:01:10,441 --> 00:01:14,313
Default phone number is used for an agent who is on no number's

18
00:01:14,313 --> 00:01:16,445
list of agents who dial from it.

19
00:01:16,445 --> 00:01:19,532
It comes from the addresses used for voice calls.

20
00:01:19,532 --> 00:01:23,741
Calls themselves still fall back to the provider's default caller ID.

21
00:01:24,203 --> 00:01:28,343
Default SMS number is the number an agent who is on no number's

22
00:01:28,343 --> 00:01:31,283
list of agents who text from it sends from.

23
00:01:31,283 --> 00:01:35,003
The messaging composer starts new conversations from it.

24
00:01:39,266 --> 00:01:45,426
On the Recording governance tab, Record every call automatically starts recording every queue

25
00:01:45,426 --> 00:01:48,599
and dialer call when it connects to an agent.

26
00:01:48,599 --> 00:01:52,581
When it is off, a call is recorded only when a workflow or

27
00:01:52,581 --> 00:01:54,386
a supervisor starts it.

28
00:01:54,859 --> 00:01:59,434
Consent model is All parties must consent, which is the default, or Single

29
00:01:59,434 --> 00:02:01,378
party consent is sufficient.

30
00:02:01,378 --> 00:02:05,609
Choose what your legal team tells you for the places you operate in.

31
00:02:06,111 --> 00:02:09,988
Tick Tell callers the call is recorded to turn on the disclosure, and

32
00:02:09,988 --> 00:02:14,071
write the words callers hear in Disclosure, for example that the call may

33
00:02:14,071 --> 00:02:16,811
be recorded for quality assurance and training.

34
00:02:17,266 --> 00:02:22,763
Say it to inbound callers speaks the disclosure before an entry point's welcome

35
00:02:22,763 --> 00:02:24,638
message, menu or queue.

36
00:02:24,638 --> 00:02:30,006
Have automated voice agents say it first does the same for an AI voice agent.

37
00:02:30,468 --> 00:02:34,051
Ask agents to say it when the caller has not heard it shows

38
00:02:34,051 --> 00:02:38,350
the disclosure and an I told the customer button in the agent workspace,

39
00:02:38,350 --> 00:02:41,988
on an outbound call or a call that skipped the announcement.

40
00:02:42,441 --> 00:02:46,177
Do not record until the caller has heard the disclosure makes a call

41
00:02:46,177 --> 00:02:50,166
start recording only once the disclosure was spoken to the caller, or the

42
00:02:50,166 --> 00:02:51,781
agent confirmed giving it.

43
00:02:52,256 --> 00:02:57,462
Retention in days says how long recordings are kept before they may be erased.

44
00:02:57,462 --> 00:02:59,321
Zero keeps them forever.

45
00:02:59,321 --> 00:03:05,146
Apply legal hold by default makes new recordings undeletable until the hold is released.

46
00:03:05,608 --> 00:03:10,528
Allow agents to pause recording shows a Pause recording button in the agent

47
00:03:10,528 --> 00:03:14,780
workspace, for example while a customer reads out a card number.

48
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:19,639
Set a maximum secure-pause window in seconds, and tick Require a reason to

49
00:03:19,639 --> 00:03:21,948
pause if the agent must say why.

50
00:03:22,409 --> 00:03:23,470
Click Save.

51
00:03:23,470 --> 00:03:28,339
Calls recorded under these rules are listed on the Call recordings page.

52
00:03:32,539 --> 00:03:37,625
On an inbound call to an entry point, the platform says the disclosure

53
00:03:37,625 --> 00:03:42,309
word for word, first, before the welcome message, menu or queue.

54
00:03:43,059 --> 00:03:46,822
A turn-based AI voice agent call gets it at the start of the

55
00:03:46,822 --> 00:03:49,729
assistant's opening line, also word for word.

56
00:03:50,479 --> 00:03:54,779
A realtime AI voice agent writes its own opening line, so it is

57
00:03:54,779 --> 00:03:57,209
told to say the disclosure first.

58
00:03:57,209 --> 00:04:00,699
Read a few call transcripts to check that it does.

59
00:04:01,449 --> 00:04:06,092
On an outbound call, or any call the caller reached without the disclosure,

60
00:04:06,092 --> 00:04:09,589
the agent reads it out and presses I told the customer.

61
00:04:09,589 --> 00:04:14,003
Each disclosure is logged on the call with the time and the words used.

62
00:04:14,003 --> 00:04:18,245
Which calls need a notice depends on where you and your callers are,

63
00:04:18,245 --> 00:04:20,309
so check with your legal team.

64
00:04:24,609 --> 00:04:30,301
The External transfer destinations tab lists the outside numbers agents and phone menus

65
00:04:30,301 --> 00:04:32,015
may transfer calls to.

66
00:04:32,015 --> 00:04:33,729
Click Add destination.

67
00:04:34,866 --> 00:04:41,262
Enter a Display name, for example After-hours answering service, and its E.164 address,

68
00:04:41,262 --> 00:04:45,526
which is the full international number with a plus sign.

69
00:04:46,408 --> 00:04:50,020
Untick Enabled to keep a row but stop offering it.

70
00:04:50,020 --> 00:04:53,438
Add a row for each destination, and click Save.

71
00:05:03,579 --> 00:05:07,849
Tick Let agents transfer to numbers that are not on this list only

72
00:05:07,849 --> 00:05:09,985
if agents may type any number.

73
00:05:09,985 --> 00:05:14,730
They also need the permission to transfer Contact Center calls externally.

74
00:05:14,730 --> 00:05:18,289
Emergency and premium-rate numbers are always refused.

75
00:05:22,526 --> 00:05:27,742
On the Secure Data Capture tab, tick Enable agent-assisted secure data capture.

76
00:05:27,742 --> 00:05:31,423
It shows Collect data securely in the agent workspace:

77
00:05:31,423 --> 00:05:36,271
the agent sends the customer a one-time link, and the customer types card

78
00:05:36,271 --> 00:05:38,296
or bank details themselves.

79
00:05:38,794 --> 00:05:45,002
Capture link lifetime sets how long the link works, from thirty to thirty-six hundred seconds.

80
00:05:45,002 --> 00:05:47,174
The default is three hundred.

81
00:05:47,629 --> 00:05:53,470
Pause recording during capture pauses the call recording while the customer enters the data.

82
00:05:53,470 --> 00:05:55,020
It is on by default.

83
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:59,490
Card numbers are checked, only the last four digits are kept, and the

84
00:05:59,490 --> 00:06:01,636
security code is never stored.

85
00:06:01,636 --> 00:06:02,649
Click Save.

86
00:06:06,849 --> 00:06:10,425
A team in a place where every party must consent turns on the

87
00:06:10,425 --> 00:06:14,909
disclosure and the setting that holds recording until the caller has heard it.

88
00:06:15,659 --> 00:06:19,812
A company with a retention policy sets the number of days, and puts

89
00:06:19,812 --> 00:06:23,169
new recordings under legal hold while a case is open.

90
00:06:23,919 --> 00:06:29,288
A support desk lists its answering service as an approved destination, so agents

91
00:06:29,288 --> 00:06:32,659
can hand off after hours without typing numbers.

92
00:06:33,409 --> 00:06:38,120
A team that takes payments turns on secure data capture and pausing, so

93
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:41,669
card details never reach the agent or the recording.

94
00:06:43,669 --> 00:06:49,679
Set the recording rules, the disclosure, the approved outside numbers and secure capture

95
00:06:49,679 --> 00:06:53,387
once, and they apply to every queue and every agent.

96
00:06:53,387 --> 00:06:55,049
Thanks for watching.

